    <!-- How it works -->
    <string name="how_it_works_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="how_step1_title">1. A call comes in</string>
    <string name="how_step1_body">Android tells the app the number that is calling, before the phone rings. Nothing is stored beyond the call currently in progress.</string>
    <string name="how_step2_title">2. You do not answer</string>
    <string name="how_step2_body">If the call rings out or you decline it, a notification appears straight away with your message ready to go.</string>
    <string name="how_step3_title">3. One tap to send</string>
    <string name="how_step3_body">Tap the action on the notification and your own messaging app opens with the number and message filled in. You press send.</string>
    <string name="how_privacy_title">What this app does not do</string>
    <string name="how_privacy_body">No call log is read and no messages are sent behind your back. Numbers are kept on this device only, for 30 minutes, purely to avoid texting the same person twice. Nothing is uploaded.</string>
    <string name="how_limits_title">Worth knowing</string>
    <string name="how_limits_body">Android only passes on calls from numbers that are not in your contacts, so saved contacts will not trigger a prompt. Calls from withheld or private numbers cannot be replied to, because there is no number to send to.</string>

